## What happened

Un-paused the ScaledObject, confirmed PVC reclaimed (20G / 60M used), ran `m-ta-prefill-knee` via
`run_cell.sh` — completed cleanly, `rc=0`, 24 min wall clock, results at
`runs/dean-20260812-152105-714/`.

Then launched `m-ta-calibration-probe` the same way, backgrounded. **A session interruption killed
the local shell mid-run**, at step [4/6] ("run"). On resume: the harness pod
(`inference-perf-mcgf3r9k`) was still `Running` on the cluster — k8s-side execution survives a local
process death — but with no local CLI process left to drive it to collection: no
`results.json`/lifecycle files had appeared under its PVC results dir
(`/requests/inference-perf-1786538941-lwy8cw_1`) after 15+ minutes, well past the profile's own
~12 min load duration. Treated as orphaned.

Ran `hack/benchmark/reset_run.py -n dhl-wva-209 --workspace . --apply`: deleted the orphaned harness
pod + its two configmaps, restarted the WVA controller and (via the ScaledObject) decode. The
harness pod is confirmed gone.

## 🚨 Unresolved — decode stuck at 10/10 idle

**Decode is sitting at 10/10 replicas with ZERO active load, ~15+ minutes after the controller
restart, and has not been observed to scale down.** No benchmark is running (harness pod deleted,
no other load source). I have not taken further action on this — no re-run, no manual scale-down,
no GPU-freeing sequence. On a shared cluster this is 10 GPUs held idle right now.

**Also unresolved:** the orphaned run's results directory
(`/requests/inference-perf-1786538941-lwy8cw_1`) is still on the PVC — `reset_run.py`'s PVC-reclaim
step only clears directories that already have a local copy under `*/results/`, and this one never
got that far, so it was correctly left in place rather than deleted blind. It was never collected
(no lifecycle-metrics files present, checked before the reset) and no local `runs/` directory exists
for it — the calibration-probe profile has not produced any usable result yet.

